{{Quote|We're farmers from Tawl.''"<br />"''Hey, there. I'm Freck.|Leia Organa and Freck|<ref name="Kenobi III" />}}
'''Freck''' was an affable [[Condluran]] who worked as a [[transport]] driver for the [[Galactic Empire]] on the [[mining]] [[planet]] [[Mapuzo]], his [[homeworld]]. Aligning with the Empire, he gained rapport with the local [[stormtrooper]]s. In [[9 BBY]], the driver came across the [[Jedi]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and the [[youngling]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]], who went under fake names and were trying to find a [[spaceport]]. The [[alien]] offered them a ride in [[Freck's truck|his]] [[FMR-385 cargo speeder]] and drove them toward a port, conversing with the pair and transporting some stormtroopers along the way.

The [[Cargo speeder|transport]] soon reached an [[Mapuzo checkpoint|inspection point]], where Freck advised the stormtroopers on duty to check out his passengers. After the [[trooper]]s did a scan of Kenobi, he [[Battle on Mapuzo|attacked]] the [[soldier]]s, using Freck as a shield to shoot one of them. The Jedi then incapacitated the Condluran and escaped with Organa.

==Biography==
===New passengers===
{{Quote|We got a bit turned around. We're looking for the nearest port. We need to get home.''"<br />"''Well, I'm going that way. Jump in.|Kenobi and Freck|<ref name="Kenobi III" />}}
During the [[Imperial Era|reign]] of the [[Galactic Empire]], the [[Condluran]]<ref name="Databank" /> Freck worked as an Imperial [[transport]] driver on<ref name="Kenobi III" /> his [[homeworld]]<ref name="SWEDK" /> [[Mapuzo]], a once-flourishing [[planet]] in the [[Mid Rim Territories]] that had been reduced to a [[mining]] wasteland by the Empire. He notably ferried around passengers such as [[stormtrooper]]s, whom he came to get along with well.<ref name="Kenobi III" /> In [[9 BBY]],<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> he was driving his [[repulsorcraft]] [[Freck's truck|truck]] towards a local [[spaceport]] after a standard transport run by a quarry when he encountered two stray civilians, the [[Youngling|younger]] of them waving for his vehicle. The pair were the fugitive [[Jedi]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and<ref name="Kenobi III" /> the ten-[[Standard year|year]]-old<ref name="Kenobi II">{{Kenobi|Part II}}</ref> [[Alderaanian]] [[Princess]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]],<ref name="Kenobi I">{{Kenobi|Part I}}</ref> the latter having been [[Search for Princess Leia|rescued]] by Kenobi after being [[Ambush on Alderaan|kidnapped]].<ref name="Kenobi II" />

[[File:FreckTrucker-OWK.png|thumb|right|300px|Freck at the controls of his transport.]]
Freck stopped for Kenobi and Organa, the latter introducing them as [[farmer]]s from [[Tawl]] named Orden and Luma and claiming that she and her "[[Parent|father]]" had gotten lost on a trip. The Condluran called their story weird, but when Kenobi explained that they were looking for the nearest spaceport, Freck offered them a ride there as he was headed that way. The elder "farmer" was reluctant to accept, but Organa took up Freck's offer and thanked him. The driver assured them that they would be at the port in no [[time]] as they climbed in. While he drove down the road, Freck had his two passengers remind him that they were from Tawl. He complimented Tawl's people for listening to the Empire. Organa subsequently professed her and Kenobi's love for the Empire, the [[alien]] agreeing and saying there was nothing wrong with a bit of order.<ref name="Kenobi III" />

Freck's transport came across a group of stormtroopers whose transport was late, prompting the Condluran to offer them a ride to their base. The driver introduced the [[trooper]]s to "Orden" and "Luma," and asked where the [[soldier]]s had come from. [[Unidentified stormtrooper 1 (Mapuzo truck)|One stormtrooper]] explained that they were being moved around to [[Hunt for Obi-Wan|search]] for a Jedi. The Condluran hoped they were not in danger, but [[Unidentified stormtrooper 2 (Mapuzo truck)|another trooper]] was confident that they would find the fugitive, unbeknownst that the Jedi was sat in the transport with them. The vehicle continued moving, one stormtrooper questioning Kenobi and Organa in the meantime. When the transport passed the troopers' base, one of them had Freck stop and thanked him as the group disembarked.<ref name="Kenobi III" />

===A very standard inspection===
{{Quote|Who are they?''"<br />"''A couple of strays I found. Thought you might wanna check em' out.''"<br />"''All right. Thanks, Freck.|A stormtrooper and Freck|<ref name="Kenobi III" />}}
[[File:FreckCheckpoint-OWK.png|thumb|left|300px|Freck speaks to the stormtrooper at the Imperial checkpoint.]]
Freck's transport soon approached an Imperial [[Mapuzo checkpoint|inspection point]], and a nervous Kenobi asked if he could get off beforehand. Freck reassured his passengers that it was just a standard inspection and stopped at the [[laser]]-gate guarded by stormtroopers. The driver got out of his transport and told [[Unidentified stormtrooper (Mapuzo checkpoint)|one trooper]] about his transport run. The stormtrooper asked about the two passengers, and Freck told the soldier they might want to inspect the pair.<ref name="Kenobi III" />

Questioning Kenobi, the troopers had an Imperial [[Viper probe droid]] do a facial scan of the Jedi, forcing him to draw a [[blaster pistol]] and begin [[Battle on Mapuzo|gunning down]] the [[probe droid]] and stormtroopers. A panicked Freck stuck close to his vehicle until Kenobi grabbed the Condluran and used him as a living shield to shoot another stormtrooper. Once the soldier was [[Death|killed]], the Jedi knocked Freck out with a [[pistol]] whip, escaping with Organa not long after.<ref name="Kenobi III" />

==Personality and traits==
{{Quote|We love the Empire.''"<br />"''Nice to meet like-minded folk. Nothing wrong with a little order, right?|Leia Organa and Freck|<ref name="Kenobi III" />}}
[[File:Freck-OWKpIII.png|thumb|right|200px|Freck was a Condluran and wore brown and gray clothes with a leather jacket.]]
Freck had a friendly demeanor and was happy to occasionally help transport hitchhikers. He supported the Empire,<ref name="Databank" /> appreciating the order it kept in [[the galaxy]] and displaying the [[Imperial crest]] on his transport. The driver kept an amicable relationship with the Imperial stormtroopers on Mapuzo and offered them transport when needed. He was also easygoing with strangers like Obi-Wan Kenobi and Leia Organa, not hesitating to give them a ride and calling the favor his pleasure. However, Freck was suspicious of the pair and Organa's story and suggested the stormtroopers check them out. Freck had [[Color|light]] skin and black [[eye]]s.<ref name="Kenobi III" />

==Equipment==
Freck donned brown and gray [[Clothing|attire]] including pants, a [[belt]] with compartments, [[Limb|fingerless]] [[glove]]s, and a [[leather]] [[jacket]].<ref name="Kenobi III" /> He drove a [[FMR-385 cargo speeder]] that featured an Imperial flag attached to the back as a sign of his loyalty.<ref name="SWEDK" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|And then the way it's rigged is that I wear this head piece ''[&hellip;]'' and when I talk, the jaw moves. And so that was what was so cool about getting to do it. ''[&hellip;]'' I would've flipped out if it was just a voice over assignment. But I got to be on set.''"<br />"[&hellip;] ''The character had your mannerisms, in your face, even though it&hellip;looked nothing like you.|Zach Braff and Donald Faison|<ref name="Fake Doctors">{{Spotify|url=episode/3iPDRRLOlxrvdA8VXOxSee?si=dcfba09d4ba54763|text=615: My Long Goodbye|quote=On this week's episode, the hospital staff learns how to say goodbye to Nurse Roberts. In the real world, Zach Braff was in a Star Wars and Donald Faison is more excited than anyone else on the planet.}}</ref>}}
[[File:FreckScreamsAtHimself.png|thumb|left|300px|Zach Braff (left) practices lines while connected with Freck's animatronic head.]]
Freck first appeared in "[[Part III]]" of the [[Disney+]] television series ''[[Star Wars: Obi-Wan Kenobi]]'', directed by [[Deborah Chow]]<ref name="Kenobi III" /> and released on [[June 1]], [[2022]].<ref name="D23">{{D23|url=everything-new-you-can-stream-on-disney-in-june-2022|text=Everything New You Can Stream on Disney+ in June 2022}}</ref> The character was portrayed in costume by [[John Rosengrant]] and voiced by [[Zach Braff]],<ref name="Kenobi III" /> known for his role in<ref name="Independent Braff">{{WebCite|url=https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/tv/news/zach-braff-obi-wan-kenobi-who-freck-b2092098.html|text=Obi-Wan Kenobi: Star Wars fans shocked to learn Zach Braff was in episode 3|author=Isobel Lewis|date=2022-06-01|work=[[Wikipedia:The Independent|''The Independent'']]|archivedate=20220615105159}}</ref> the television series [[Wikipedia:Scrubs (TV series)|''Scrubs'']],<ref name="Slashfilm Scrubs">{{WebCite|url=https://www.slashfilm.com/946119/scrubs-burnout-sent-zach-braff-running-away-from-tv-work|text=Scrubs Burnout Sent Zach Braff Running Away From TV Work|author=Sandy Schaefer|date=2022-07-29|work=[[Wikipedia:/Film|''/Film'']]|archivedate=20220804232610}}</ref> with other individuals also controlling Freck's eyebrows and eyes.<ref name="DTG Featurette" /> Freck's costume included an animatronic head<ref name="Jedi's Return">''[[Obi-Wan Kenobi: A Jedi's Return]]''</ref> that functioned on what Braff stated was seventy motorized servos, with additional head movement features being remote-controlled by two puppeteers.<ref name="Fake Doctors" /> In a practice run with the head set, the actor recited lines intended for the scene<ref name="Jedi's Return" /> where Kenobi used him as a shield. Those lines did not make it into the finished episode.<ref name="Kenobi III" />

A significant portion of ''Obi-Wan Kenobi'' was shot on a set known as "[[Wikipedia:StageCraft|The Volume]],"<ref name="Jedi's Return" /> which Braff was shown around by Chow,<ref name="Fake Doctors" /> as Freck's actor had previously starred in the director's debut film.<ref name="DTG Featurette" /> The scenes with Freck, though, were filmed in a desert ranch<ref name="Fake Doctors" /> in [[Wikipedia:Iwin, California|Irwin]], [[Wikipedia:California|California]]<ref name="DTG Featurette">{{HomeVideoCite|set=Obi-Wan Kenobi: The Complete Series|featurette=Designing the Galaxy}}, "[[Part VI]]" {{C|director's commentary from [[Obi-Wan Kenobi: The Complete Series|''The Complete Series'']]}}</ref>, where the actor, by his own account, remarked to the director that the show's viewers would think the set was still The Volume.<ref name="Fake Doctors" /> While the landscape was all natural features, the surrounding mountains and additional special effects were added in post-production to all of Freck's scenes.<ref name="DTG Featurette" /> According to Braff, Rosengrant, while in costume for the character, had to have cool air pumped into the suit due to the hot weather. During the shooting of Freck's scenes, the actor would recite his lines behind cameras with the headpiece on as part of the animatronic's choreography<ref name="Fake Doctors" /> and a microphone was attached to his head piece<ref name="Instagram">{{Instagram|username=zachbraff|url=p/CeRkBB9vFXK|name=[[Zach Braff]]|date=2022-06-01|quote=Obi-Wan Kenobi: Episode 3 is a good one I hear. 😇|archiveurl=https://archive.is/PYYhf}}</ref> to project his speech for the filmed interaction<ref name="Jedi's Return" /> with Kenobi, Organa, and the stormtroopers.<ref name="Kenobi III" />

[[File:FreckBehindTheScenes.png|thumb|right|320px|Braff, director Deborah Chow, and Josh Rosengrant (as Freck) on the Mapuzo set.]]
Braff was surprised that, because of the secrecy behind ''Obi-Wan Kenobi''{{'s}} production, his "sides"&mdash;scripts he used for his part in the episode and hoped to take with him as a souvenir&mdash;were taken away by staff at the end of the day.<ref name="Fake Doctors" /> After the release of "Part III," fans reportedly mistook Braff's voice of Freck as that of the actor [[Wikipedia:Seth Rogen|Seth Rogen]].<ref name="Independent Braff" /> Braff himself discussed his role on his podcast with fellow ''Scrubs'' actor [[Donald Faison]],<ref name="Fake Doctors" /> who was also part of ''[[Star Wars]]'' as the character [[Hype Fazon]] in the [[2018]] animated series ''[[Star Wars Resistance]]''.<ref name="Resistance Cast">{{SW|url=news/star-wars-show-resistance-cast|text=Meet the Cast of ''Star Wars Resistance'' on ''The Star Wars Show''}}</ref> Expressing his joy about being in the show, he wished for there to be an action figure or [[LEGO]] set including him.<ref name="Fake Doctors" /> The [[2023]] [[Topps]] card set [[2023 Topps Star Wars: Obi-Wan Kenobi|2023 Topps ''Star Wars: Obi-Wan Kenobi'']] included a card with concept art of Freck driving his truck.<ref name="OWKTopps">{{Topps|set=2023 Topps Star Wars: Obi-Wan Kenobi|subset=Concept Art|cardname=CA-8 Chapter 3|link=https://www.tcdb.com/ViewCard.cfm/sid/365364/cid/21460642}}</ref>

